# Ask Riz, the chat panel in the header. Copy to `.env.local` for development and
# set the same keys in the Vercel project's environment variables for deployment.
#
# The diagram itself needs none of these. With all four unset the app builds, deploys and
# renders exactly as it did before the panel existed; the panel answers that it is not
# configured on this deployment. Nothing else degrades.

# Required. The panel's only outbound call.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional. Defaults to claude-haiku-4-5, which ties Sonnet 5 at 8/8 on `npm run eval`
# and costs 2.6x less. Anthropic's slugs move faster than this repository does, so this
# is here to avoid a deploy for a model swap -- run the eval before using it.
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=

# Optional. Defaults to 2000. Questions per day across *everyone*, which is the only
# limit that bounds the invoice -- the per-IP windows price abuse rather than cap it,
# since addresses are rented by the thousand. Roughly $59/day at the worst a single
# question can cost on the Haiku default, nearer $30 in ordinary use.
RIZ_GLOBAL_DAILY=

# Required in production, ignored in development. /api/ask is unauthenticated and sits in
# front of a billed API key, so the route refuses to serve rather than serve unlimited when
# these are missing -- see lib/ratelimit.ts. Vercel's Upstash integration provisions
# KV_REST_API_URL / KV_REST_API_TOKEN instead, and both spellings are read.
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
